If there is a cycle in this graph, say $i \to j \to i$, then we must have $x_i \le x_j$ and $x_j \le x_i$, which implies $x_i = x_j$.
If there are no cycles, the graph is a forest (a collection of trees). However, the edges are directed $i \to A_i$. Since each node has exactly one outgoing edge (to $A_i$), the graph is a collection of components where each component consists of a cycle with some trees rooted on the cycle nodes, with edges directed towards the cycle.
