Initially, the $i$-th alien has $A_i$ stones.
The $i$-th alien becomes an adult exactly $i$ years later.
When an alien becomes an adult, every adult who currently has at least one stone gives one stone to the newly adult alien.
We need to find the number of stones each alien has after $N$ years.

Let's denote the number of stones alien $i$ has at time $t$ as $C_i(t)$.
Initially, at $t=0$, $C_i(0) = A_i$.
The events happen at integer years $t=1, 2, \ldots, N$.
At year $t$, the $t$-th alien becomes an adult.
The condition for giving a stone is: "every adult who has at least one stone".
Who are the adults at year $t$?
An alien $j$ is an adult at year $t$ if $j \le t$.
