"Choose 2K mochi and form K pairs. For each pair, place one mochi on top of the other".
So we need to select $2K$ indices from $[L, R]$ and partition them into $K$ pairs $(u_j, v_j)$ such that $A_{u_j} \le A_{v_j} / 2$. Note that since $A$ is sorted, if we pick a set of $2K$ indices, say $x_1 < x_2 < \dots < x_{2K}$, then $A_{x_1} \le A_{x_2} \le \dots \le A_{x_{2K}}$.
If we pair $A_{x_1}$ with $A_{x_{2K}}$, $A_{x_2}$ with $A_{x_{2K-1}}$, etc., we check if $A_{x_j} \le A_{x_{2K-j+1}}/2$.
